IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`
IMPORT `sfa-interests`

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation "version in force from 29/6/2026 to 20/10/2026"
-- (a rendering, not the official text). Layer 1, Part 7 Division 1, sections 130 to 132: application and interpretation of the Division,
-- who must comply and the Authority's exemption and extension powers. Written from the text alone.
--
-- How to read a result (the rule of 2026-10-29, as the keel reads it): JUST TRUE is yes; JUST FALSE is "the text says no in its own words";
-- NOTHING is "the text does not say" (a list not closed, an "includes", a scope limit with no "only", a power or term outside the sources).
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. Every branch that answers a no carries a FALSE-kind comment; every "not covered" carries a NOTHING-kind comment.

§ `s 130: application and interpretation of Division 1`

-- src:27946 | 130.—(1) This section has effect for the purposes of this Division
-- src:27947 | but does not affect the operation of any other provision of this Act.
@ref s 130(1) (src:27946-27947)
GIVEN
    `the provision being read is in Division 1 of Part 7` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision being read one in Division 1 of Part 7 of the Act (sections 130 to 137G)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130(1) section 130 has effect for the purposes of Division 1 and does not affect any other provision` MEANS
    IF `the provision being read is in Division 1 of Part 7`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not affect the operation of any other provision of this Act"

-- "A reference to a corporation" in Division 1 is a reference to a LISTED body: paragraph (a) a company, paragraph (b) another corporation with a primary listing.
-- The text defines the reference ("is a reference"), so a body in neither paragraph is outside it: the combining function answers JUST FALSE.
-- src:27951 | (2) A reference to a corporation is a reference —
-- src:27953 | (a) to a company any or all of the shares in which are listed for
-- src:27954 | quotation on the official list of an approved exchange; or
@ref s 130(2)(a) (src:27951-27954)
GIVEN
    `the body is a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a company (as section 2(1) defines "company")?
    `any or all of the shares in the body are listed for quotation on the official list of an approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any or all of the shares in the body listed for quotation on the official list of an approved exchange?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130(2)(a) the body is a company listed on an approved exchange` MEANS
    IF `the body is a company` AND `any or all of the shares in the body are listed for quotation on the official list of an approved exchange`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to a company any or all of the shares in which are listed for quotation on the official list of an approved exchange"

-- src:27956 | (b) to a corporation (not being a company, or a collective
-- src:27957 | investment scheme constituted as a corporation) any or all
-- src:27958 | of the shares in which are listed for quotation on the official
-- src:27959 | list of an approved exchange, such listing being a primary
-- src:27960 | listing.
@ref s 130(2)(b) (src:27956-27960)
GIVEN
    `the body is a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a company (as section 2(1) defines "company")?
    `the body is a collective investment scheme constituted as a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a collective investment scheme constituted as a corporation?
    `any or all of the shares in the body are listed for quotation on the official list of an approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any or all of the shares in the body listed for quotation on the official list of an approved exchange?
    `the listing is a primary listing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that listing a primary listing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130(2)(b) the body is a corporation other than a company with a primary listing` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the body is a company`) AND (NOT `the body is a collective investment scheme constituted as a corporation`) AND `any or all of the shares in the body are listed for quotation on the official list of an approved exchange` AND `the listing is a primary listing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to a corporation (not being a company, or a collective investment scheme constituted as a corporation) any or all of the shares in which are listed for quotation on the official list of an approved exchange, such listing being a primary listing"

-- src:27951 | (2) A reference to a corporation is a reference —
-- src:27953 | (a) to a company any or all of the shares in which are listed for
-- src:27954 | quotation on the official list of an approved exchange; or
-- src:27956 | (b) to a corporation (not being a company, or a collective
-- src:27957 | investment scheme constituted as a corporation) any or all
-- src:27958 | of the shares in which are listed for quotation on the official
-- src:27959 | list of an approved exchange, such listing being a primary
-- src:27960 | listing.
@ref s 130(2) (src:27951-27960)
GIVEN
    `the body is within paragraph (a) of section 130(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 130(2)(a) answer for the body (a company listed on an approved exchange)? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the body is within paragraph (b) of section 130(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 130(2)(b) answer for the body (a corporation, not a company, with a primary listing)? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130(2) the body is a corporation for the purposes of Division 1` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the body is within paragraph (a) of section 130(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the body is within paragraph (b) of section 130(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`the body is within paragraph (a) of section 130(2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`the body is within paragraph (b) of section 130(2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A reference to a corporation is a reference"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a limb the caller could not answer is not read as a no

-- src:27964 | (3) In relation to a corporation the whole or a portion of the share
-- src:27965 | capital of which consists of stock, an interest of a person in any such
-- src:27966 | stock is deemed to be an interest in an issued share in the corporation
-- src:27967 | having attached to it the same rights as are attached to that stock.
@ref s 130(3) (src:27964-27967)
GIVEN
    `the share capital of the corporation consists wholly or partly of stock` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the whole or a portion of the share capital of the corporation consist of stock?
    `the person has an interest in the stock` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have an interest in that stock?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130(3) the person's interest in stock is deemed to be an interest in an issued share` MEANS
    IF `the share capital of the corporation consists wholly or partly of stock` AND `the person has an interest in the stock`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In relation to a corporation the whole or a portion of the share capital of which consists of stock, an interest of a person in any such stock"

-- "A reference to a member": two limbs, each a "means" definition.
-- src:27974 | (4) A reference to a member —
-- src:27976 | (a) in relation to a company, means a person who is a member
-- src:27977 | of the company under section 19(6) of the Companies
-- src:27978 | Act 1967; and
@ref s 130(4)(a) (src:27974-27978)
GIVEN
    `the body is a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a company (as section 2(1) defines "company")?
    `the person is a member of the company under section 19(6) of the Companies Act 1967` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a member of the company under section 19(6) of the Companies Act 1967?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130(4)(a) the person is a member of the company` MEANS
    IF `the body is a company` AND `the person is a member of the company under section 19(6) of the Companies Act 1967`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in relation to a company, means a person who is a member of the company under section 19(6) of the Companies Act 1967"

-- src:27980 | (b) in relation to a corporation (other than a company), means
-- src:27981 | any person equivalent to a member of a company.
@ref s 130(4)(b) (src:27980-27981)
GIVEN
    `the body is a corporation other than a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a corporation that is not a company?
    `the person is equivalent to a member of a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person equivalent to a member of a company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130(4)(b) the person is a member of a corporation other than a company` MEANS
    IF `the body is a corporation other than a company` AND `the person is equivalent to a member of a company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in relation to a corporation (other than a company), means any person equivalent to a member of a company"

-- src:27974 | (4) A reference to a member —
-- src:27976 | (a) in relation to a company, means a person who is a member
-- src:27977 | of the company under section 19(6) of the Companies
-- src:27978 | Act 1967; and
-- src:27980 | (b) in relation to a corporation (other than a company), means
-- src:27981 | any person equivalent to a member of a company.
@ref s 130(4) (src:27974-27981)
GIVEN
    `the person is a member of the corporation within paragraph (a) of section 130(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 130(4)(a) answer (a member of a company)? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the person is a member of the corporation within paragraph (b) of section 130(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 130(4)(b) answer (a person equivalent to a member, in a corporation other than a company)? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130(4) the person is a member of the corporation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the person is a member of the corporation within paragraph (a) of section 130(4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the person is a member of the corporation within paragraph (b) of section 130(4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`the person is a member of the corporation within paragraph (a) of section 130(4)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`the person is a member of the corporation within paragraph (b) of section 130(4)` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A reference to a member"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a limb the caller could not answer is not read as a no

-- s 130(5): "To avoid doubt, section 4 applies". The keel's s 4 is called, not restated. Division 1 speaks of "securities or securities-based
-- derivatives contracts", not of units in a collective investment scheme, so a thing that is neither is outside the sentence.
-- src:27985 | (5) To avoid doubt, section 4 applies for the purpose of determining
-- src:27986 | whether a person has an interest in securities or securities‑based
-- src:27987 | derivatives contracts under this Division.
@ref s 130(5) (src:27985-27987)
GIVEN
    `the thing is a security or a securities-based derivatives contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a security or a securities-based derivatives contract (as section 2(1) defines those)?
    `the person has an interest by the route of s 4(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for s 4(1) answer (authority to dispose of, or control the disposal of, the thing)? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the person has an interest by the route of s 4(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for s 4(3) answer (a trust)? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the person has an interest by the route of s 4(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for s 4(4) answer (a corporation the person directs or controls)? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the person has an interest by the route of s 4(5)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for s 4(5) answer (a corporation in which the person and associates hold 20% of the votes)? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the person has an interest by the route of s 4(7)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for s 4(7) answer (one of the circumstances in subsection (7))? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the person has an interest by the route of s 4(8)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for s 4(8) answer (joint holding)? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the interest is to be disregarded under section 4(10)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 4(10) the interest is to be disregarded` answer for this interest? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130(5) the person has an interest in the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts under Division 1` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a security or a securities-based derivatives contract`
    THEN `s 4 the person has an interest in the securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units` TRUE `the person has an interest by the route of s 4(1)` `the person has an interest by the route of s 4(3)` `the person has an interest by the route of s 4(4)` `the person has an interest by the route of s 4(5)` `the person has an interest by the route of s 4(7)` `the person has an interest by the route of s 4(8)` `the interest is to be disregarded under section 4(10)`
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "whether a person has an interest in securities or securities-based derivatives contracts under this Division"

-- s 130(6): the conclusive presumption of awareness. It is a rule about WHEN a person "becomes aware" for the five provisions it names, so it is encoded twice:
-- as a yes/no (is the person presumed aware) and as the day from which the person is taken to have been aware (the earlier of the actual day and the day
-- reasonable diligence would have given awareness: fork register entry A1).
DECLARE `s 130(6) kind of person` IS ONE OF
    `s 130(6) an individual`
    `s 130(6) a body corporate or an unincorporated association other than a partnership`
    `s 130(6) a limited liability partnership`
    `s 130(6) a partnership`

-- src:27991 | (6) For the purposes of sections 133(3)(b)(i), 135(2)(b), 136(1),
-- src:27992 | 137(1) and 137E(6), a person is conclusively presumed to have been
-- src:27993 | aware of a fact or occurrence at a particular time —
-- src:27995 | (a) of which he or she would, if he had acted with reasonable
-- src:27996 | diligence in the conduct of his or her affairs, have been
-- src:27997 | aware at that time;
-- src:27999 | (b) where the person is a body corporate or unincorporated
-- src:28000 | association (other than a partnership), of which its officer
-- src:28001 | would, if he or she had acted with reasonable diligence in
-- src:28002 | the conduct of its affairs, have been aware at that time;
-- src:28004 | (c) where the person is a limited liability partnership, of which
-- src:28005 | its partner or manager would, if he or she had acted with
-- src:28006 | reasonable diligence in the conduct of its affairs, have been
-- src:28007 | aware at that time; or
-- src:28009 | (d) where the person is a partnership, of which its partner
-- src:28010 | would, if he or she had acted with reasonable diligence in
-- src:28011 | the conduct of its affairs, have been aware at that time.
@ref s 130(6) (src:27991-28011)
GIVEN
    `the provision being read is one of sections 133(3)(b)(i), 135(2)(b), 136(1), 137(1) and 137E(6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision being read one of sections 133(3)(b)(i), 135(2)(b), 136(1), 137(1) and 137E(6) (or one of their counterparts in Divisions 2 and 3 of Part 7)?
    `the kind of person` IS A `s 130(6) kind of person` @desc Is the person an individual, a body corporate or unincorporated association other than a partnership, a limited liability partnership, or a partnership?
    `the person would, if the person had acted with reasonable diligence in the conduct of the person's affairs, have been aware of the fact or occurrence at that time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the person, if the person had acted with reasonable diligence in the conduct of the person's affairs, have been aware of the fact or occurrence at that time?
    `an officer of the body would, if the officer had acted with reasonable diligence in the conduct of its affairs, have been aware of the fact or occurrence at that time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would an officer of the body corporate or unincorporated association, if the officer had acted with reasonable diligence in the conduct of its affairs, have been aware of the fact or occurrence at that time?
    `a partner or manager of the limited liability partnership would, if acting with reasonable diligence in the conduct of its affairs, have been aware of the fact or occurrence at that time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would a partner or manager of the limited liability partnership, if acting with reasonable diligence in the conduct of its affairs, have been aware of the fact or occurrence at that time?
    `a partner of the partnership would, if acting with reasonable diligence in the conduct of its affairs, have been aware of the fact or occurrence at that time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would a partner of the partnership, if acting with reasonable diligence in the conduct of its affairs, have been aware of the fact or occurrence at that time?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130(6) the person is conclusively presumed to have been aware of the fact or occurrence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the provision being read is one of sections 133(3)(b)(i), 135(2)(b), 136(1), 137(1) and 137E(6)`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of sections 133(3)(b)(i), 135(2)(b), 136(1), 137(1) and 137E(6)"
        IF `the person would, if the person had acted with reasonable diligence in the conduct of the person's affairs, have been aware of the fact or occurrence at that time`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`the kind of person` EQUALS `s 130(6) a body corporate or an unincorporated association other than a partnership`) AND `an officer of the body would, if the officer had acted with reasonable diligence in the conduct of its affairs, have been aware of the fact or occurrence at that time`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`the kind of person` EQUALS `s 130(6) a limited liability partnership`) AND `a partner or manager of the limited liability partnership would, if acting with reasonable diligence in the conduct of its affairs, have been aware of the fact or occurrence at that time`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`the kind of person` EQUALS `s 130(6) a partnership`) AND `a partner of the partnership would, if acting with reasonable diligence in the conduct of its affairs, have been aware of the fact or occurrence at that time`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the presumption extends awareness to what reasonable diligence would have shown; it does not say a person without such a ground was unaware

-- src:27991 | (6) For the purposes of sections 133(3)(b)(i), 135(2)(b), 136(1),
-- src:27992 | 137(1) and 137E(6), a person is conclusively presumed to have been
-- src:27993 | aware of a fact or occurrence at a particular time —
-- src:27995 | (a) of which he or she would, if he had acted with reasonable
-- src:27996 | diligence in the conduct of his or her affairs, have been
-- src:27997 | aware at that time;
@ref s 130(6) (the day from which the person is taken to have been aware) (src:27991-27997)
GIVEN
    `the day the person actually became aware of the fact or occurrence` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the person actually become aware of the fact or occurrence?
    `the earliest day on which the person, or the person's officer, partner or manager, would have become aware of it if acting with reasonable diligence` IS A DATE @desc What is the earliest date on which the person, or the person's officer, partner or manager as the case may be, would have become aware of the fact or occurrence if acting with reasonable diligence in the conduct of their affairs?
GIVETH A DATE
`s 130(6) the day from which the person is taken to have been aware` MEANS
    IF `the earliest day on which the person, or the person's officer, partner or manager, would have become aware of it if acting with reasonable diligence` LESS THAN `the day the person actually became aware of the fact or occurrence`
    THEN `the earliest day on which the person, or the person's officer, partner or manager, would have become aware of it if acting with reasonable diligence`
    ELSE `the day the person actually became aware of the fact or occurrence`

-- s 130(7): "officer" and "partner", for section 130 itself (the presumption above).
-- src:28015 | (7) In this section —
-- src:28017 | “officer” —
-- src:28019 | (a) in relation to a body corporate, means a director,
-- src:28020 | member of the committee of management, chief
-- src:28021 | executive officer, manager, secretary or other similar
-- src:28026 | officer of the body, and includes a person purporting
-- src:28027 | to act in any such capacity; or
@ref s 130(7) "officer" (a) (src:28015-28027)
GIVEN
    `the person is a director, member of the committee of management, chief executive officer, manager, secretary or other similar officer of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a director, member of the committee of management, chief executive officer, manager, secretary or other similar officer of the body corporate?
    `the person purports to act in any such capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person purport to act in any such capacity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130(7) "officer" (a) the person is an officer of a body corporate` MEANS
    IF `the person is a director, member of the committee of management, chief executive officer, manager, secretary or other similar officer of the body corporate` OR `the person purports to act in any such capacity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in relation to a body corporate, means a director, member of the committee of management, chief executive officer, manager, secretary or other similar officer of the body"

-- src:28029 | (b) in relation to an unincorporated association (other
-- src:28030 | than a partnership), means the president, the
-- src:28031 | secretary, or a member of the committee of the
-- src:28032 | association, or a person holding a position analogous
-- src:28033 | to that of president, secretary or member of the
-- src:28034 | committee, and includes a person purporting to act in
-- src:28035 | such capacity;
@ref s 130(7) "officer" (b) (src:28029-28035)
GIVEN
    `the person is the president, the secretary or a member of the committee of the association, or holds a position analogous to one of those` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the president, the secretary or a member of the committee of the unincorporated association (other than a partnership), or does the person hold a position analogous to one of those?
    `the person purports to act in any such capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person purport to act in any such capacity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130(7) "officer" (b) the person is an officer of an unincorporated association` MEANS
    IF `the person is the president, the secretary or a member of the committee of the association, or holds a position analogous to one of those` OR `the person purports to act in any such capacity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in relation to an unincorporated association (other than a partnership), means the president, the secretary, or a member of the committee of the association"

-- src:28037 | “partner” includes a person purporting to act as a partner.
@ref s 130(7) "partner" (src:28037-28037)
GIVEN
    `the person purports to act as a partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person purport to act as a partner?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130(7) "partner" the person is a partner` MEANS
    IF `the person purports to act as a partner`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes a person purporting to act as a partner" is an extension of the ordinary word, not a closed list

§ `s 131: who must comply with Division 1, and the Authority's exemption and extension`

-- src:28044 | 131.—(1) The obligation to comply with this Division extends to
-- src:28045 | all natural persons, whether resident in Singapore or not and whether
-- src:28046 | citizens of Singapore or not, and to all entities, whether formed,
-- src:28047 | constituted or carrying on business in Singapore or not.
@ref s 131(1) (src:28044-28047)
GIVEN
    `the person is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a natural person?
    `the person is an entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an entity (as section 2(1) defines "entity")?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(1) the obligation to comply with Division 1 extends to the person` MEANS
    -- Residence in Singapore and citizenship are immaterial ("whether resident in Singapore or not and whether citizens of Singapore or not"), so neither is an input.
    IF `the person is a natural person` OR `the person is an entity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text names "all natural persons" and "all entities"; a person who is neither is not addressed

-- src:28051 | (2) This Division extends to acts done or omitted to be done outside
-- src:28052 | Singapore.
@ref s 131(2) (src:28051-28052)
GIVEN
    `the act or omission was done or omitted to be done outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act done, or the thing omitted, outside Singapore?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(2) Division 1 extends to the act or omission` MEANS
    IF `the act or omission was done or omitted to be done outside Singapore`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This Division extends to acts done or omitted to be done outside Singapore"; an act in Singapore is not this subsection's subject

-- src:28056 | (3) The Authority may exempt any person or class of persons from
-- src:28057 | any or all of the provisions of this Division.
@ref s 131(3) (src:28056-28057)
GIVEN
    `the Authority has exempted the person, or a class of persons including the person, from the provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority exempted the person, or a class of persons that includes the person, from the provision?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(3) the person is exempt from the provision of Division 1` MEANS
    IF `the Authority has exempted the person, or a class of persons including the person, from the provision`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "The Authority may exempt any person or class of persons from any or all of the provisions of this Division"; whether it has done so is the Authority's act

-- src:28061 | (4) The Authority may by written notice impose on a person
-- src:28062 | exempted under subsection (3), or by regulations impose on a class of
-- src:28063 | persons exempted under that subsection, such conditions or
-- src:28064 | restrictions as the Authority thinks fit and the person or persons
-- src:28065 | must comply with such conditions or restrictions.
@ref s 131(4) (src:28061-28065)
GIVEN
    `the person is exempted under section 131(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority exempted the person under section 131(3)?
    `the Authority has imposed a condition or restriction on the person by written notice, or on the class of persons by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority imposed a condition or restriction on the person by written notice, or on a class of persons including the person by regulations?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(4) the exempted person must comply with the condition or restriction` MEANS
    IF `the person is exempted under section 131(3)` AND `the Authority has imposed a condition or restriction on the person by written notice, or on the class of persons by regulations`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person exempted under subsection (3)" with a condition or restriction imposed under subsection (4)

DECLARE `s 131 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 131 contravene a condition or restriction imposed under subsection (4)`

-- s 131(4) is a "must comply" with no time limit, so as a MUST it has no breach path (NOTES.md, "Rules with no breach path"); the same duty is written as the
-- prohibition it amounts to (SHANT, derived from the flat negative: ruling N2 of 2026-11-04) so that a trace can reach the offence of subsection (5).
-- src:28061 | (4) The Authority may by written notice impose on a person
-- src:28062 | exempted under subsection (3), or by regulations impose on a class of
-- src:28063 | persons exempted under that subsection, such conditions or
-- src:28064 | restrictions as the Authority thinks fit and the person or persons
-- src:28065 | must comply with such conditions or restrictions.
-- src:28069 | (5) Any person who contravenes any condition or restriction
-- src:28070 | imposed under subsection (4) shall be guilty of an offence and
-- src:28071 | shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $50,000 and, in
-- src:28072 | the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding
-- src:28077 | $5,000 for every day or part of a day during which the offence
-- src:28078 | continues after conviction.
@ref s 131(4) and (5) (the prohibition) (src:28061-28078)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 131 action`
`s 131(4) and (5) the exempted person shall not contravene a condition or restriction` MEANS
    PARTY Individual "the exempted person"
    SHANT `s 131 contravene a condition or restriction imposed under subsection (4)`
    LEST BREACH BY Individual "the exempted person" BECAUSE "contravened a condition or restriction imposed under section 131(4): an offence under section 131(5)"

-- src:28069 | (5) Any person who contravenes any condition or restriction
-- src:28070 | imposed under subsection (4) shall be guilty of an offence and
-- src:28071 | shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $50,000 and, in
-- src:28072 | the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding
-- src:28077 | $5,000 for every day or part of a day during which the offence
-- src:28078 | continues after conviction.
@ref s 131(5) (src:28069-28078)
GIVEN
    `the person contravenes a condition or restriction imposed under section 131(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person contravene a condition or restriction imposed under section 131(4)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(5) the person is guilty of an offence of contravening a condition or restriction` MEANS
    IF `the person contravenes a condition or restriction imposed under section 131(4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): SPLIT-SITE (i) the text says who is guilty ("Any person who contravenes any condition or restriction"), not that a person who does not is innocent

-- src:28069 | (5) Any person who contravenes any condition or restriction
-- src:28070 | imposed under subsection (4) shall be guilty of an offence and
-- src:28071 | shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $50,000 and, in
-- src:28072 | the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding
-- src:28077 | $5,000 for every day or part of a day during which the offence
-- src:28078 | continues after conviction.
@ref 2 s 131(5) (the penalty) (src:28069-28078)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 131(5) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    -- a fine not exceeding $50,000 and, for a continuing offence, a further fine not exceeding $5,000 a day after conviction; no imprisonment is stated, so 0
    Penalty OF 50000, 0, FALSE, 5000

-- s 131(6): the Authority may extend the time, on application. The "may" is gated by "on the application of a person required to give a notice":
-- the grant-and-power ruling (the grant limit) says NOTHING when the gate fails; the periods ruling (b) would say JUST FALSE. SPLIT-SITE (ii), fork line B2.
-- src:28082 | (6) The Authority may, on the application of a person required to
-- src:28083 | give a notice under this Division, extend, or further extend, the time
-- src:28084 | for giving the notice.
@ref s 131(6) (src:28082-28084)
GIVEN
    `a person required to give a notice under Division 1 has applied to the Authority for an extension of the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a person required to give a notice under Division 1 applied to the Authority to extend the time for giving the notice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 131(6) the Authority has power to extend, or further extend, the time for giving the notice` MEANS
    IF `a person required to give a notice under Division 1 has applied to the Authority for an extension of the time`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): SPLIT-SITE (ii) "may, on the application of a person required to give a notice under this Division"; the gate is not a "where" and the function is named for a power

-- src:28082 | (6) The Authority may, on the application of a person required to
-- src:28083 | give a notice under this Division, extend, or further extend, the time
-- src:28084 | for giving the notice.
@ref 2 s 131(6) (the last day after an extension) (src:28082-28084)
GIVEN
    `the last day for giving the notice under the section` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for giving the notice under the section (before any extension)?
    `the Authority has extended the time on the person's application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority, on the person's application, extended the time for giving the notice?
    `the last day to which the Authority has extended the time` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day to which the Authority has extended the time (leave any date if there is no extension)?
GIVETH A DATE
`s 131(6) the last day for giving the notice, as extended on the person's application` MEANS
    IF `the Authority has extended the time on the person's application` AND (`the last day to which the Authority has extended the time` GREATER THAN `the last day for giving the notice under the section`)
    THEN `the last day to which the Authority has extended the time`
    ELSE `the last day for giving the notice under the section`

-- s 132 (the Authority's power to extend the scope of the Division by regulations): regulation-making power, so a coverage row `inert` (reason 2), no code.
